   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ הָעׇרְלָה וְכִלְאֵי הַכֶּרֶם – מִצְטָרְפִין זֶה עִם זֶה. רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן אוֹמֵר: אֵין מִצְטָרְפִין.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» «The fruit of a tree during the first three years after its planting [orla]» (see Leviticus 19:23), «and diverse kinds,»i.e., grain sown «in a vineyard» (see Deuteronomy 22:9) «join together» to constitute the requisite measure to prohibit a mixture that they are mixed into. This applies when the volume of the permitted produce is less than two hundred times the prohibited produce. «Rabbi Shimon says: They do not join together.»"
  }
